    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23415" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δᾰναοί</span></b> , οἱ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Danaäns,</i>
			subjects of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δάναος,</span> king of Argos,
			but in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.42
			</span></i>, al., for <i>the Greeks</i> generally (but expl. as 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεκροί</span>
			 (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάνος</span> (B)), <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				247.49
			</span></i>): Com.
				Sup.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαναώτατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					259
				</span></i>
			:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαναΐδαι</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶν</span>, οἱ, <i>the sons</i> or <i>descendants of
				Danaus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				466
			</span></i>:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαναΐδες</span></b> , αἱ, <i>his
			daughters,</i> name of a play of <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i></div>
